# Folder Structure

Use `@/` alias (`src/`) for all internal imports.

## Layout

```
src/
├── app/                    # App shell: providers, router only
├── assets/
├── components/
│   ├── common/             # Shared UI primitives (Button, Input)
│   └── layout/             # AppLayout, ProtectedRoute
├── config/                 # env.ts, routes.ts
└── features/
    ├── shared/             # Cross-feature: api client, api types, utils
    │   ├── api/
    │   ├── types/
    │   └── utils/
    ├── auth/
    ├── user-management/
    ├── task-management/
    ├── team-management/
    ├── analytics/
    ├── dashboard/
    └── settings/
```

## Feature module shape (required)

Every feature folder follows the **user-management** pattern:

```
features/<feature-name>/
├── _api/           # HTTP calls only (axios)
├── _components/    # UI + route pages for this feature
├── _hooks/         # React hooks
├── _service/       # Business logic wrapping _api
├── _stores/        # Context, zustand, or state slices
├── _types/         # Feature-specific TypeScript types
├── _utils/         # Feature-specific helpers
└── index.ts        # Public barrel — only export what other features need
```

## Layer rules

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| `_api` | Raw HTTP — no business logic |
| `_service` | Orchestration, transforms, storage side-effects |
| `_hooks` | React state + calls `_service` |
| `_components` | Presentational UI and page components |
| `_stores` | Global/feature state (AuthProvider lives in auth/_stores) |
| `_types` | Types owned by this feature |
| `_utils` | Pure helpers scoped to this feature |

## Import rules

- Import features via `@/features/<name>` barrel (`index.ts`)
- Pages live in `_components/` (e.g. `UsersPage.tsx` in user-management)
- Shared HTTP client: `@/features/shared`
- Never import another feature's `_api` directly — use its `_service` or barrel
- `app/router.tsx` wires routes; imports pages from feature barrels

## Do not

- Use unprefixed folders (`api/`, `hooks/`) inside features — always `_api`, `_hooks`, etc.
- Put domain logic in `src/pages/`, `src/lib/`, or `src/contexts/` — use features
- Duplicate types across features — import from the owning feature barrel
